their relationships with those agents or managers&nbsp;
are how people are allowed to come into pitch or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.480
how a screenplay will end up on your desk. If&nbsp;
I'm a screenwriter at home who has an idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.460
nine times out of ten because there's always that&nbsp;
one but nine times out of ten you're going to need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.920
some kind of representation to get you through&nbsp;
that door and most of that is because you don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.900
want just anybody able to send something out&nbsp;
somewhere because then legally it becomes an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:44.340
