so it's like a really fine line do you want to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:53.640
something exactly do you not want to but there&nbsp;
can be ways to exit situations gracefully and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:58.680
I haven't always been the best at that and and&nbsp;
I know I'm sure other people haven't either and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:04.500
and it can really follow you and it's one of the&nbsp;
reasons that I I left the business it's one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:09.660
the reasons so I've told this story before but I&nbsp;
left the business so that I could go do musical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:14.580
theater and dance companies which was always&nbsp;
a dream of mine but at this age I'm thinking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:20.700
I'm in my career that dream is gone so that dream&nbsp;
kind of came back around at a moment of transition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:26.280
for me anyway I felt like I had learned everything&nbsp;
that I needed to learn from this particular place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:31.560
and I wanted to then take those skills&nbsp;
somewhere else because I didn't feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:37.080
comfortable at this place and even though I was&nbsp;
26 and had been told to be seen and not heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:44.700
I didn't feel like I needed to go in and make&nbsp;
declarations about what I was feeling I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:49.740
born in the 80s your feelings stay at home what&nbsp;
I mean you don't come into your job talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:53.580
how people are making you feel who cares get&nbsp;
the job done if you don't want to be here go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:59.400
somewhere else so I was in a place of deciding&nbsp;
to go somewhere else and then then this whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:04.500
opportunity to do something different came up and&nbsp;
I did it but when I came back I also came back at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:10.680
36 or seven so it's a whole decade later I'm a&nbsp;
totally different woman I'm far more confident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:14.700
than I was and that's one of the reasons when I&nbsp;
came back I knew that I wanted to be at a place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:20.400
that needed me a place that was going to hear my&nbsp;
voice a place that was going to respect what I had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:26.580
to give I did not want to be receiving a paycheck&nbsp;
to just be a number in the room what I mean like I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:30.900
have things to offer so if you're going to hire me&nbsp;
then you're going to get those things and now I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:34.920
not walking into a room looking for permission to&nbsp;
speak I'm here because you should want to hear my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:40.080
voice if not why are you paying me why am I here&nbsp;
but that's different because I have these decades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:45.240
of experience now so I walk into a room totally&nbsp;
differently but at 26 I would I don't even know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:50.040
if I thought about going to HR I don't even know&nbsp;
if I considered it now I can look back and go well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:55.620
if I had I might have started a problem because I&nbsp;
know about the history and how it was 20 years ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.880 --> 00:17:01.920
but at this age I would probably talk to HR&nbsp;
because I believe in protocol so I believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:06.660
that you have to inform people of something so&nbsp;
that they can have an opportunity to try to fix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:10.620
it because if you don't inform them of it you just&nbsp;
keep it inside then you're going to come to work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:13.860
frustrated every day and no one else is going to&nbsp;
know why you're frustrated because they don't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:19.800
you have a problem so either you speak to your&nbsp;
supervisor about your problem if you can't speak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:23.580
to them you go to the person above them if you&nbsp;
can't speak to them you talk to HR whoever it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:27.840
that you're supposed to talk to to try to solve&nbsp;
the problem first if this is a place where you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:33.300
actually want to be and want to thrive and if you&nbsp;
then can't figure it out or if it does backfire on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:37.560
you because it because it can get very political&nbsp;
then you start to figure out what your exit is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:41.940
but again like you said that exit can be graceful&nbsp;
it doesn't have to be well I'm leaving because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:46.020
of this and you did that and blah blah blah if&nbsp;
you get an exit interview and they ask you why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:50.400
you're leaving give them the facts on why you're&nbsp;
leaving and then leave but it doesn't have to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:56.940
doesn't have to be a moment where you're giving&nbsp;
it to the man what I mean on your way out so when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.940 --> 00:18:04.080
I did do my exit interview I did inform HR at&nbsp;
that time what my whole experience was and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:09.720
she said to me oh my gosh why didn't you come to&nbsp;
us sooner what I mean but for me it was it just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:13.200
hadn't crossed my mind I hadn't even thought&nbsp;
about it but I did want to give the feedback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:18.660
on the way out because I didn't want someone&nbsp;
else to have my experience I wanted to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:23.400
sure that even in their marketing and this&nbsp;
is where maybe I was stepping over line but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.940
like even in their marketing stop calling&nbsp;
it a program it's not a program it's a job&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:34.680
you need people who are ready to do the job and&nbsp;
if they're not ready to do the job then you need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:40.140
a program that teaches them that guides them&nbsp;
that gives them a mentor that tells them some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:44.700
of the stuff that they need to do because again&nbsp;
I came in thinking I'm just going to be writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:48.840
some great coverage and possibly get to work&nbsp;
with the writing staffs and blah blah blah I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:54.840
had no idea all of the rest of it even existed&nbsp;
and how could I being on the outside even coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:59.100
from film school and so I needed them to have&nbsp;
that feedback so from what I know there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:03.900
only one more one more cohort after me and then&nbsp;
the program stopped it had nothing to do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:09.960
me and what what happened but I think a lot of&nbsp;
programs like that no longer exist now and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:13.500
kind of ended over the last decade and even some&nbsp;
of the fellowships that we know really well have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:19.080
been talking about ending because money is being&nbsp;
moved around etc etc but I do think that it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:24.120
it was necessary because it's very&nbsp;
hard to go from assistant to executive.

